<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mauritius</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mauritius is an island nation in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>, about 2,000 kilometres off the south-east coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. Uninhabited until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> settled it in 1638, it was ruled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> as Isle de France from 1715 and by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> from 1810, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> plantations worked first by enslaved and then by indentured Indian labourers shaped its population. It became independent in 1968 and a republic in 1992.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mauritius.jpg" alt="Mauritius" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zscout370 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Mauritius.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
